 V2 corrects the independently identified legitimate-metadata inventory blocker in immutable V1 f81b. Only VERIFIED and the exact physically colocated VERIFIED-MODEL-MANIFEST.json argument with original 7f53 SHA are allowed beyond the eleven official files. Both metadata bytes are included in the actual teacher asset inventory, final all_files rehash, and exact saved-teacher comparison; VERIFIED content is never treated as a PASS. Unknown extra files, symlinks, wrong manifest names/SHA, and outside-directory manifest used to allow a local copy are rejected. Original V1 source/review/tests are preserved.
+
+V3 additionally joins the actual native SHARDED payload to its actual externally manifest-pinned HF index and all referenced shard full SHA. It checks complete index/header key inventory, FP32 safeheader extents/global shapes, then exact torch.equal for every rank-local Shard(0) slice of every tensor, including tied lm_head and norms, with no tolerance. Output adds hf_all_rank_slices_exact=true, hf_files (actual index/shard path to SHA map), and each rank model_hf_slice_exact=true / model_hf_slice_keys (all actual 435 keys). A changed-positive comparison to the original base alone is no longer accepted as cross-format identity. Old V1/V2 evidence remains immutable. CPU fixtures explicitly include a changed HF slice with fresh file hashes, near-identical norm difference, missing/duplicate/extra keys, tied-head mismatch, and path escape rejection. No actual first-five data has been inspected.
